<!--
	The types this system knows, and what each one is.

	A type is not a filename extension. It is a name in a tree: public.png conforms to
	public.image, which conforms to public.data, which conforms to public.item. Asking
	whether something is an image is asking whether its type conforms to public.image, and
	the answer is right for a kind of image nobody had heard of when the question was
	written.

	The identifiers in the public domain are the ones every system that does this uses, and
	so are the ones third parties own: com.adobe.pdf is Adobe's name for a PDF wherever it
	is read. What this system invents for itself is under org.fractalmicro.

	UTTypeDescription holds a key rather than words, looked up in Localizable.strings the
	way every other piece of text is. The Kind column of a window is this description.

	Declared here, in the framework's own resources, and copied into its Info.plist when the
	volume is laid out. An application declares its own the same way, in its bundle, and
	Launch Services reads them all into one database.
-->
